      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Daphne sits on Mobile Bay’s eastern shore and is part of the Daphne‑Fairhope‑Foley metro area that ranks in the nation’s top 10 by Site Selection Magazine.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daphne%2C_Alabama",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The city’s historic Village Point Park Preserve offers birdwatching and a view of the bay, reflecting Daphne’s blend of nature and heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.discoverdaphne.org/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A 19th‑century Methodist church built in 1858 now houses a charming museum that tells the town’s story.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.discoverdaphne.org/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The area has been inhabited since at least 9,000 BCE, making Daphne one of Alabama’s oldest continuously populated regions.",
